---@alias gcp.cloudchannel_v1.GoogleCloudChannelV1CustomerConstraintsPromotionalOrderTypesItemEnum "PROMOTIONAL_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NEW_UPGRADE"|"TRANSFER"|"PROMOTION_SWITCH"

---@alias gcp.cloudchannel_v1.GoogleCloudChannelV1CustomerConstraintsPromotionalOrderTypesItemEnumList gcp.cloudchannel_v1.GoogleCloudChannelV1CustomerConstraintsPromotionalOrderTypesItemEnum[]

---@alias gcp.cloudchannel_v1.GoogleCloudChannelV1CustomerCustomerAttestationStateEnum "CUSTOMER_ATTESTATION_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"EXEMPT"|"NON_EXEMPT_AND_INFO_VERIFIED"

---@alias gcp.cloudchannel_v1.GoogleCloudChannelV1CustomerList gcp.cloudchannel_v1.GoogleCloudChannelV1Customer[]

---Configuration for how a reseller will reprice a Customer.
---@class gcp.cloudchannel_v1.GoogleCloudChannelV1CustomerRepricingConfig
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name of the CustomerRepricingConfig. Format: accounts/{account_id}/customers/{customer_id}/customerRepricingConfigs/{id}.
---@field repricingConfig? gcp.cloudchannel_v1.GoogleCloudChannelV1RepricingConfig Required. The configuration for bill modifications made by a reseller before sending it to customers.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp of an update to the repricing rule. If `update_time` is after RepricingConfig.effective_invoice_month then it indicates this was set mid-month.

---@alias gcp.cloudchannel_v1.GoogleCloudChannelV1CustomerRepricingConfigList gcp.cloudchannel_v1.GoogleCloudChannelV1CustomerRepricingConfig[]

---A representation of usage or invoice date ranges.
---@class gcp.cloudchannel_v1.GoogleCloudChannelV1DateRange
---@field invoiceStartDate? gcp.cloudchannel_v1.GoogleTypeDate The earliest invoice date (inclusive). If this value is not the first day of a month, this will move it back to the first day of the given month.
---@field usageStartDateTime? gcp.cloudchannel_v1.GoogleTypeDateTime The earliest usage date time (inclusive). If you use time groupings (daily, weekly, etc), each group uses midnight to midnight (Pacific time). The usage start date is rounded down to include all usage from the specified date. We recommend that clients pass `usage_start_date_time` in Pacific time.
---@field usageEndDateTime? gcp.cloudchannel_v1.GoogleTypeDateTime The latest usage date time (exclusive). If you use time groupings (daily, weekly, etc), each group uses midnight to midnight (Pacific time). The usage end date is rounded down to include all usage from the specified date. We recommend that clients pass `usage_start_date_time` in Pacific time.
---@field invoiceEndDate? gcp.cloudchannel_v1.GoogleTypeDate The latest invoice date (inclusive). If this value is not the last day of a month, this will move it forward to the last day of the given month.

---Represents a single component of the total discount applicable on a Price.
